A denial claude enforces and this build cannot express. deniedMcpServers entries carry
exactly one of serverName, serverCommand or serverUrl; a serverCommand entry blocks by
argv, which does not map onto the server NAMES the parity comparison is stated in.

The stdio server is why this fixture answers UNMEASURED rather than merely dropping
the denial. An argv-keyed denial can only reach a server declared with a command, so
one sitting beside an http-only dir subtracts provably nothing and leaves the set
knowable; it is the sketchy entry that puts a server in reach of this file's denial and
makes "which of these names survives" the question this build cannot answer. Reported
as the configured set, this dir would be credited with a server it blocks.

It is rich's settings.json and .claude.json with that denial swapped in and that server
added, so a test pinning the MCP axis is about the denial rather than about unrelated
drift. Two differences from rich are deliberate and neither is incidental: this one,
and the local-scope entry named scratch-cmddenial that rich/README describes.
